course: dictionary
lesson: 11352
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Zip is one of them. The context, meaning the words around it, tells you which meaning to use. «Zip up your coat, it is cold outside.» Here zip is a verb: you close the coat with a zip.
explain: «The cheetah zipped across the grass.» Zipped is a verb that means moved very fast. The clue is the word across: something moving quickly goes across the grass. Always ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then check it by putting that meaning in place of the word.
explain: A zip can also be a noun, a thing: the fastener with two rows of small teeth. «You learn your postcode or ZIP code, because it helps letters to be delivered quickly.» Here ZIP code is a postcode used in the United States. Look at the words next to zip, such as «zip your lip», «zip line» or «zip file», because they often change the meaning.
fact: Zip is a noun and a verb: a zip is a fastener, and to zip means to close it or to move very fast.
fact: «Zip your lip» means be quiet.
fact: A zip has two rows of teeth on cloth tapes, and the slider pushes them together.
fact: In computing, to zip files means to squash them into a smaller file.
fact: In American English, a zip fastener is called a zipper.
exercise: «Zip up your coat, it is cold outside.» What does zip mean here? | *To close with a zip | To squash files into a smaller file | To move very fast | Nothing at all
exercise: «The cheetah zipped across the grass.» What does zipped mean? | *To move very fast | Zero, nothing at all | To close with a zip | A fastener with two rows of small teeth
exercise: «Zip your lip for a minute, please.» What does zip your lip mean? | Sing loudly | Open your mouth wide | Put on a warm coat | *Be quiet
test: «She pulled the zip slowly so it would not catch her skin.» What is a zip in this sentence? | To move very fast | *A fastener with two rows of small teeth | A zoo for tigers | To squash files into a smaller file
test: «Pack the photos into one zip file to send them.» In computing, what does zip file mean? | A cloth tape with teeth | *A file squashed into a smaller size | A file that moves very fast | A file with a broken tooth
exam: «Ella zipped up her bag before she ran for the bus.» Which meaning of zip fits here? | A squashed computer file | *To close with a zip | To move very fast | Nothing at all
